title start
kind: todo
tags: todo viewer
Todo page: tasks with marks, notes and answers
title end

paragraph start
Use a todo page for tasks. Each task is one short paragraph. A todo line under its start line marks it open or done, and sections group tasks by theme.
paragraph end

section start
title start
Open tasks
title end

paragraph start
todo: write the install guide and test it on a clean machine before Friday
Install the tool on a clean machine and run the checker on one page.
answer start
for: qadd5fe
asked: Is this one action that can be finished and checked?
Yes. One install and one check, finished when the checker prints clean.
answer end
paragraph end

paragraph start
todo: waiting for Anna to name the second operating system
Test the install on a second operating system.
comment start
Anna may have a spare laptop. Ask her again on Monday. A comment inside a block belongs to that block.
comment end
paragraph end
section end

section start
title start
Done
title end

comment start
These two tasks came from the same review, so one comment covers both. Put the blocks inside the comment.

paragraph start
todo: done viewer fixed, block names now sit on the left
Move the block names to the left edge.
paragraph end

paragraph start
todo: done contracts now show on every page
Show the contracts without a flag.
paragraph end
comment end
section end

section start
title start
Ideas
title end

paragraph start
A task with no todo line is just a note. Keep each task under forty words, and split it when it needs more.
paragraph end

comment start
The questions under each block come from the todo type. Fill them in with an answer block; the answer is matched to its question by ID, so reordering questions never breaks it.
comment end
section end
